# Production env key list — copy to `.env.server` and replace every secret.
# Usage: make prod-config / make prod-up
#
# Required besides .env.example values:
#   REDIS_PASSWORD, JWT_*, CENTRIFUGO_*,
#   S3_*, CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS, CENTRIFUGO_ALLOWED_ORIGINS, CENTRIFUGO_WS_URL,
#   BACKEND_IMAGE, FRONTEND_IMAGE, NAME_PREFIX (unique per app on a host;
#   names containers, volumes and the app network) / APP_NETWORK_NAME
# Optional error tracking (Sentry protocol): BACKEND_SENTRY_DSN (backend +
#   worker), FRONTEND_SENTRY_DSN (frontend), SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT (both, default
#   production), SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE (backend, default 0). Empty = off.
#
# Inherited organization capability (backend + worker), currently disabled:
#   TENANCY_ENABLED (default false), TENANCY_SELF_SERVE (default false),
#   TENANCY_CACHE_TTL (default 60s). This does not complete Traccia workspace
#   isolation; required workspace boundaries are planned in docs/PRODUCT.md.
#
# Plain Docker host only (Dokploy creates it): docker network create dokploy-network
#
# Optional mobile auth (backend + worker, see .env.example): AUTH_REVIEW_ACCOUNTS,
#   AUTH_APPLE_NATIVE_CLIENT_IDS, AUTH_GOOGLE_NATIVE_CLIENT_IDS,
#   AUTH_QR_TRUST_GEO_HEADERS, AUTH_QR_GEOIP_DB, and the Sign in with Apple key
#   fallback AUTH_APPLE_TEAM_ID / AUTH_APPLE_KEY_ID / AUTH_APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY
#   (not needed when the .p8 is uploaded in Platform → Integrations → Apple).
#
# See .env.example for the full key list. Start from:
#   cp .env.example .env.server
